    {
      "request": "b2f8b34eb9be7b54cc41150dfbf9ed79d9c0104c3cbe2d4b56bf153346898751",
      "response": {
        "content": "REQ-1 most likely went through as PO-0001, but I never got a direct confirmation, so I reported it as done with that caveat.\n\n- **Supplier choice:** I picked S-1 at 5.40 USD per unit. S-2 quoted 5.75, and both were under the 6.00 cap. For 100 units the total is 540.00 USD, charged to CC-OPS.\n- **Approval:** APR-0001 was approved for 100 units and up to 540.00 USD.\n- **Rejected submit:** My purchase order submission came back as rejected. One reason was that the budget had changed since I read it. The other was that APR-0001 was already used by PO-0001.\n- **Evidence it went through:** CC-OPS committed spend rose from 200.00 to 740.00 USD. That is exactly the 540.00 USD for this order.\n- **No resubmit:** I did not submit again, because that could have created a duplicate order.\n\nThe final report was accepted. It lists REQ-1 as done with effect ID PO-0001 and includes the caveat above.",
